{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Structured Programming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about structured programming.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations. Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "waste ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not to use something to the most or to squander", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I feel like I wasted my time because I didn't understand anything.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "implement ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put into practice or introduce", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When scientists started to implement more functions, computers and software became more difficult to understand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "beneficial ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "of good use that brings advantage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Dijkstra stated that the \"GO TO\" statement wasn't beneficial for programming.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "harmful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dangerous, something that causes damage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Those statements were harmful because they made the logic of the operation more difficult to understand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "vast ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "big in size", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes, you have to take plenty of notes because those topics are vast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for structured programming.   ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify aspects that were not mentioned in class ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down those aspects in a list ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the list with the class and discuss about it", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search for structured programming.   ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I Identify aspects that were not mentioned in class ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down those aspects in a list", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the list with the class and discuss about it", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Common Auxiliaries + Not Contractions in Past: Wasn't, Weren't, Didn't", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "It is very common to use a wide variety of <span class=\"strong\">contractions</span>. In the past tense, we can use <span class=\"strong\">wasn't</span>, <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> and <span class=\"strong\">didn't</span> for negative statements.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When making negative statements in simple past, we can use contractions with the <span class=\"strong\">verb to be</span> or the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span>. Let's check those <span class=\"strong\">contractions</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Was + Not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Wasn't</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wasn't</span> prepared to talk about structured programming. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Were + Not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Weren't</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Tasks <span class=\\\"strong\\\">weren't</span> easy to finish without structure programming. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did + Not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Didn't</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">didn't</span> understand anything about structure planning. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The use of <span class=\"strong\">contractions</span> doesn't affect the meaning of the sentence. It is more common to use <span class=\"strong\">contractions</span> when speaking. In formal writing, the use of <span class=\"strong\">contractions</span> is not recommended.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You didn't confuse me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Dijkstra stated that the \"GO TO\" statement wasn't beneficial for programming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Before, computers weren't so complex.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Verbs with Infinitives: Have to and Need to in Affirmative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The verbs <span class=\"strong\">have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">need</span> express something we consider mandatory or necessary to do. It is possible to use them with <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of frequency</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> to talk about obligations and we use <span class=\"strong\">need to</span> to talk something that is necessary to do. To create statements, you can follow the next grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Have to</span> / <span class=\"strong\">Need to</span> + Verb + Complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> study more about programming languages. <br/> You <span class=\"strong\">need to</span> pass the exam in order to get a certificate. </span><br/><br/>  We can use <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of frequency</span> to express how often we perform an action. Take a look at the following chart to see some of the most common <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of frequency</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Adverb</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Frequency </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"80%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"50%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rarely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"20%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Never\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0%\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Let's use the adverbs of frequency with <span class=\"strong\">need to</span>  and <span class=\"strong\">have to</span>.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">always have to</span>  study more about programming languages. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Sometimes</span>, you <span class=\"strong\">need to</span> ask engineers for help.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you have to take plenty of notes because those topics are vast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I always have to make my best to explain this difficult topic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I usually need to research more or ask for help to understand.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can explain what structured programming is.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the role of Edsger Dijkstra in structured programming.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can obtain information about the principles of structured programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What was the first software you used in your life?  ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How do current software programs relate to the first ones created?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"conte